      en: "The exam does not test what YOU would do, but what PMI’s ideal project manager would do: proactive, transparent, serving the team and value. Cardinal rules: 1) understand before acting — gathering information and root-cause analysis precede any action; 2) handle it yourself before escalating — escalation is a last resort (or an explicit governance obligation); 3) people before process — talk to the person involved before documenting, sanctioning or bypassing; 4) value before deliverables; 5) no hidden sacrifice — neither quality, nor compliance, nor transparency is traded for schedule.",
