      en: "• Beta PERT = (O + 4M + P)/6, NOT the average of the three: the “simple average” option is a systematic distractor.\n• “Management cuts the estimate 20% to motivate the team”: always wrong — negotiate scope or resources, not the numbers.\n• Story points ≠ person-days: any option converting them directly or comparing them across teams is wrong.\n• Hidden padding ≠ contingency reserve: the former is concealment, the latter a documented, managed provision.\n• A highly precise bottom-up estimate on a still poorly defined scope gives FALSE precision, not a better estimate: method precision never compensates for a real lack of scope information.\n• Demanding a “definitive” estimate (−5/+10%) at initial framing is unrealistic: that precision level is only reachable after detailed scope decomposition, not before.",
